86408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "628c5962-9540-54e0-a743-71b039507ef9" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=2 e^{- y},\\qquad 2 x - 3>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2 x - 3}\\cdot 2 \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}2 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{2}{2 x - 3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{2 x - 3} &=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fef22b4-1658-51c4-9d88-3a9f9308339c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577186} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea23ce8-56d6-5036-b822-761465ad590a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fef22b4-1658-51c4-9d88-3a9f9308339c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577186} :answer-field/id #uuid "096de02a-e114-565a-97e3-fbb6d888f0b9" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a047d6-d21d-54fd-bd52-edd9989ba98c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577187} {:answer/id #uuid "6c090d77-8107-5ce4-844f-f3f7a0f9ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c090d77-8107-5ce4-844f-f3f7a0f9ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #