\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{1}{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}4 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4}{e^{\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc87408-521e-5ff3-81ad-d12b8336cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577198} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5cc371-1e31-5af0-b590-b0e123a69dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc87408-521e-5ff3-81ad-d12b8336cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577198} :answer-field/id #uuid "121ca29b-ff12-50d2-a3bf-d408737a7afb" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a41b91-a3e8-52ba-ba25-b21d70c222a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577182} {:answer/id #uuid "83796f1a-f177-5bfb-9026-ee69e4168ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83796f1a-f177-5bfb-9026-ee69e4168ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577210} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a41cff6-b393-54f3-8621-68b284e47ac3" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34812337-a6dc-5027-b32a-f77570a6742e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577191} {:answer/id #uuid "45dea541-accf-5351-87dd-ce5e1122aee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34812337-a6dc-5027-b32a-f77570a6742e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577191} :answer-field/id #uuid "f98785b4-f724-5466-bb66-b99672465add" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d568f072-4f2d-5062-9df6-070b49ac30ab" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-\\sin(4x)\\cdot 4 \\\\ &=- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 2 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} &\\not\\equiv - 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217f4b64-d556-5199-9baf-43913544c7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577188} {:answer/id #uuid "88a48421-c948-52f1-bbed-84c1398d5096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88a48421-c948-52f1-bbed-84c1398d5096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577211} :answer-field/id #uuid "621ceb6c-b367-53bb-a1d7-504317392b55" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c941adf7-363e-506c-bec4-f379ec73747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577215} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1cdf16-a724-5637-b8f8-f29be5bb16c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c941adf7-363e-506c-bec4-f379ec73747e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577215} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dbe8bcd-6fff-57bd-988f-7e5cada4b731" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0af4a76a-c609-5072-9c28-07593351d9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577181} {:answer/id #uuid "3c00e4ed-d238-578a-8252-db6ba353adf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c00e4ed-d238-578a-8252-db6ba353adf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577193} :answer-field/id #uuid "d23c64dd-d8d6-5fdd-aced-ed924c331a79" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f69906ca-c5a8-50c6-b2ca-cd97ea4fc11a" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\cos(2x) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} &\\not\\equiv \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899c8195-18d6-577b-b497-a767c94fd9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577260} {:answer/id #uuid "e2508ccb-9092-5e29-b099-8e7a5e084a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899c8195-18d6-577b-b497-a767c94fd9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577260} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f0af7fc-a183-5432-8aa6-90714a3b16d0" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "309fec51-949f-5aa2-9e56-7b7ab05da2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577240} {:answer/id #uuid "836fdad7-3107-5b59-aeb6-c89477568106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "309fec51-949f-5aa2-9e56-7b7ab05da2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577240} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5507b0-90fc-51e0-a572-7ef2530af52e" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- 16 x^{4}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144251c2-9709-58d2-a1b8-7cfd771764df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577234} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb86bec-67e2-5f02-9a89-601383bc948d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144251c2-9709-58d2-a1b8-7cfd771764df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577234} :answer-field/id #uuid "b172cfd8-30ff-5646-9672-925044e7beef" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08c38953-f704-56cc-b3e1-73f07fd4a27c" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{5 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 4 x^{5}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x^{4}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 4 x^{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 4 x^{5}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-4\\cdot 5 x^{4} \\\\ &=- 20 x^{4} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 16 x^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=- 4 x^{5}$ and $y\\prime=- 20 x^{4}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 20 x^{4} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 4 x^{5}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 20 x^{4} &=- 20 x^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=- 4 x^{5}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096fa35e-adf0-56ac-96a6-f0d914653171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577233} {:answer/id #uuid "702a4e6a-ff6b-521c-a157-521109dc3428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "096fa35e-adf0-56ac-96a6-f0d914653171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577233} :answer-field/id #uuid "14afc219-898a-5f29-a488-e9de74e30fc4" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32789ef3-e490-5af2-bd76-0010e6157806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577241} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cf98a3-b5f3-5f58-b6f2-9fa7361a79c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5cf98a3-b5f3-5f58-b6f2-9fa7361a79c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577272} :answer-field/id #uuid "71481ca8-e7c8-5dea-9ec6-cf7e74d010d1" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577255} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c95be75-7cdb-5526-881d-fedce4e80ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577253} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6eca7f-19f6-5353-ba11-c792dfc27b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa6eca7f-19f6-5353-ba11-c792dfc27b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577279} :answer-field/id #uuid "b240868a-780d-52d0-9567-8e15eefe7db1" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1eb042b7-4390-5cc3-b683-bdc64a6141fc" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{5 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 8 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 8 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-8\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 16 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=- 8 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 16 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\not\\equiv - 40 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=- 8 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c669eed-d1b3-5024-8bdb-7d4214af06fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577243} {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577252} :answer-field/id #uuid "194c9336-9913-5379-9825-4dba3d9209d2" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c96df9-a022-5